<title>JAPAN: Yamaichi fires employees over suspicious deals.</title>
<headline>Yamaichi fires employees over suspicious deals.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yamaichi Securities Co Ltd said on Monday it had dismissed four employees at its branch in Shinjuku, central Tokyo, over what it called suspicious stock transactions.</p>
<p>The brokerage house dismissed a senior branch official in July over suspicions that stock transactions had been made using the names of clients without permission, a Yamaichi spokesman said.</p>
<p>Three other employees at the branch were also dismissed in August and September as they were suspected of being involved in the transactions, he said.</p>
<p>The spokesman declined to comment further, saying the case had been referred to police.</p>
</text>
